1
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:02,840
Jianguo.

2
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:05,640
Busy?

3
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,400
Just in time.

4
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,439
Got something to talk to you about.

5
00:01:09,959 --> 00:01:10,920
What do you want with me?

6
00:01:11,319 --> 00:01:11,799
Come on.

7
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:12,840
We can talk right here.

8
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:14,599
Nothing major.

9
00:01:20,319 --> 00:01:20,719
Sit.

10
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:25,359
Jianguo, Jianguo.

11
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,319
Can't you stay out of trouble for once?

12
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,439
You always have to stir up trouble.

13
00:01:30,959 --> 00:01:32,359
I didn't do anything, Bro Meng.

14
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:33,879
You didn't do anything?

15
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,599
Would I be looking for you if you hadn't?

16
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:37,239
How should I know?

17
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,560
How could you not?

18
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:40,840
Yesterday in town,

19
00:01:41,159 --> 00:01:43,280
around 11:00 p.m., there was a fight.

20
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,719
An out-of-town fellow got his head cracked open.

21
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,000
He's in the hospital right now.

22
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:52,400
You should know about this, right?

23
00:01:52,439 --> 00:01:54,079
No, I really don't know anything about it.

24
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,000
I was in Dongguan delivering aluminum windows.

25
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I only got back this morning.

26
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:57,719
If you don't believe me,

27
00:01:57,719 --> 00:01:59,120
you can ask the window factory.

28
00:01:59,239 --> 00:01:59,879
Go check it out.

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,359
Isn't that why I'm asking you?

30
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:03,560
I'll go check after we talk.

31
00:02:04,519 --> 00:02:05,239
By the way,

32
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,519
the guy who got beaten said

33
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:08,919
the man who attacked him

34
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:12,439
was nearly 1.9 meters tall,

35
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:14,879
and bald.

36
00:02:15,479 --> 00:02:16,360
Now tell me,

37
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:19,520
who else around here looks like that?

38
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,319
That's not fair to say, Bro Meng.

39
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,759
Just because I'm tall and bald,

40
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,439
you can't just pin this on me.

41
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:28,680
That's not right.

42
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,240
All right, all right.

43
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,759
Whether I'm right or not isn't up to me.

44
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:31,680
How about this?

45
00:02:32,879 --> 00:02:34,319
He's at the hospital right now.

46
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,280
Come with us.

47
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:37,960
We'll go to the hospital

48
00:02:38,719 --> 00:02:40,759
and let him take a look at you in person.

49
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:42,000
Up for it?

50
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,439
Why wouldn't I be? Let's go.

51
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:46,159
Let's go.

52
00:02:49,159 --> 00:02:50,039
Boss! Boss!

53
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,960
I think I left my phone at the station.

54
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:53,879
All right, all right.

55
00:02:53,879 --> 00:02:55,360
Hospital first. It's not far.

56
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,800
I've got to go get it.

57
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,520
My girlfriend might be looking for me.

58
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:01,599
Look at you, acting like a hen that lost its egg.

59
00:03:01,599 --> 00:03:02,719
It'll be quick, Boss.

60
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,639
Make it quick, then.

61
00:03:05,199 --> 00:03:05,639
Okay.

62
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,000
Hurry up, hurry up, hurry up.

63
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:12,919
Come on.

64
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,439
Take a look at our place.

65
00:03:18,639 --> 00:03:19,439
Come.

66
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:20,960
Please have a seat.

67
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,479
You're back.

68
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,080
All set.

69
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:37,960
Bro Meng.

70
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:40,000
Wait, what are you guys doing?

71
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,159
Aren't we going to the hospital to ID someone?

72
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:43,280
Since you're already here,

73
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,080
think carefully.

74
00:03:45,439 --> 00:03:46,800
What have you been up to lately?

75
00:03:49,159 --> 00:03:49,960
Xiao Chang.

76
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,400
He came all this way.

77
00:03:52,439 --> 00:03:53,479
Pour him some water.

78
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,560
Didn't you hear me?

79
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,360
Boss...

80
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Pour some water!

81
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,039
For our guest, come on.

82
00:04:10,639 --> 00:04:12,280
What are you daydreaming about?

83
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:18,519
And me too!

84
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:28,639
Your turn.

85
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,959
Stand up.

86
00:04:56,199 --> 00:04:57,519
Try on this vest.

87
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:58,879
Put it on.

88
00:04:59,079 --> 00:04:59,879
No, I...

89
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:02,560
Put it on, let me see.

90
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:06,959
For the mugshot.

91
00:05:07,399 --> 00:05:09,480
Hold on, let me fix it.

92
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,160
I still have to go home and cook.

93
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,839
Stand straight. For the photo.

94
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:17,879
Done yet?

95
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,040
Can I go now?

96
00:05:26,319 --> 00:05:27,920
This way, this way.

97
00:05:34,199 --> 00:05:34,839
Move.

98
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,040
Buddy,

99
00:05:42,079 --> 00:05:43,079
you're a veteran.

100
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,120
You should know

101
00:05:46,839 --> 00:05:48,160
what Chen Jun is wearing

102
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,720
and what it means.

103
00:05:51,319 --> 00:05:52,079
You get it, right?

104
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:53,920
And remember:

105
00:05:55,199 --> 00:05:58,199
confessing versus being turned in—

106
00:05:58,199 --> 00:05:59,519
those are two different things.

107
00:06:00,399 --> 00:06:01,160
Believe it or not,

108
00:06:02,879 --> 00:06:04,959
Chen Jun might very well

109
00:06:05,399 --> 00:06:06,600
get time off for turning you in.

110
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:09,879
We brought you here—

111
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:12,560
think we'd do that without solid proof?

112
00:06:13,839 --> 00:06:14,839
I'm clean.

113
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,639
Better if you are.

114
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,360
Please.

115
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:26,600
Bro Meng.

116
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,360
Why the change of venue?

117
00:06:28,439 --> 00:06:29,240
Sit.

118
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,920
Find it strange?

119
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:37,879
I don't get it.

120
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:50,920
Here.

121
00:06:55,519 --> 00:06:56,439
Your clothes.

122
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,079
Extra-large.

123
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:02,959
Look.

124
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,959
On these clothes,

125
00:07:07,199 --> 00:07:08,399
there's the victim's blood.

126
00:07:19,959 --> 00:07:21,120
On the button,

127
00:07:22,199 --> 00:07:23,560
we also lifted

128
00:07:24,319 --> 00:07:25,399
your fingerprints.

129
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,519
We all know each other here.

130
00:07:40,879 --> 00:07:42,519
Talk or don't, it's up to you.

131
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,480
I'll turn him in.

132
00:08:00,399 --> 00:08:01,360
Made up your mind?

133
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,120
Sit down.

134
00:08:19,079 --> 00:08:19,680
Go ahead.

135
00:08:21,519 --> 00:08:22,360
I'll talk.

136
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,519
I'll confess.

137
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,959
Get someone from out of town to do it.

138
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,759
Once it's done, they never come back.

139
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,919
You should be in the clear.

140
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:39,919
How much can you pay?

141
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:43,279
How much does this usually cost?

142
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,679
I don't know the going rate.

143
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:50,759
Five thousand.

144
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,320
You want someone dead.

145
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:54,159
Five thousand?

146
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:55,879
No one does it for that.

147
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,240
At least 50,000.

148
00:09:01,879 --> 00:09:03,480
I may know a lot of people,

149
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,039
but someone who can handle this

150
00:09:07,039 --> 00:09:08,120
is no ordinary guy.

151
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:10,120
10,000.

152
00:09:11,679 --> 00:09:12,919
I can pay 10,000 at most.

153
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,360
Not a penny more.

154
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,720
If it's 10,000,

155
00:09:21,559 --> 00:09:22,240
that works.

156
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,320
But that's only for one person.

157
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,480
Do you want to kill Chen Changhe,

158
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:30,879
or his wife?

159
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,000
Chen Changhe.

160
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:33,440
No.

161
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,080
I want to kill his wife.

162
00:09:37,679 --> 00:09:40,960
I want Chen Changhe to watch his wife die.

163
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,360
I want him to suffer.

164
00:09:43,679 --> 00:09:44,679
Ruthless.

165
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:46,679
Kill the body, torment the soul.

166
00:09:48,559 --> 00:09:50,480
I'll scrape the money together.

167
00:09:50,759 --> 00:09:51,960
Find the guy first.

168
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,919
Bring him to meet me once you find him.

169
00:09:55,639 --> 00:09:56,600
Better not.

170
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,639
So you don't get implicated.

171
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,600
I won't even tell him who hired him.

172
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,559
It's to protect you.

173
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:05,600
You get it?

174
00:10:07,759 --> 00:10:09,039
You're pretty professional.

175
00:10:10,639 --> 00:10:11,320
Here you go.

176
00:10:14,559 --> 00:10:15,720
Still three-fifty?

177
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:16,559
Yeah, that's right.

178
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,120
Here.

179
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:22,879
Thanks.

180
00:10:23,559 --> 00:10:24,000
I'm off.

181
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:24,519
Take care.

182
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,120
Bro,

183
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,480
the guy's here. We can make our move.

184
00:10:43,919 --> 00:10:45,080
Go wherever you need to go.

185
00:10:45,919 --> 00:10:47,440
Don't stay in the village.

186
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,320
Make some noise

187
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:50,720
and make sure you're seen.

188
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,759
Stop, stop, stop.

189
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,000
What the...

190
00:12:34,159 --> 00:12:35,120
No, wait...

191
00:12:38,399 --> 00:12:40,679
Didn't I tell you to get someone from out of town?

192
00:12:41,159 --> 00:12:42,320
You did it yourself?

193
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,000
Who'd take it for that little money?

194
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:45,919
The pros wouldn't take it.

195
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,600
Let's go.

196
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,039
Come on!

197
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,399
I killed her!

198
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:11,399
I killed her!

199
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,960
Take off your clothes.

200
00:13:34,159 --> 00:13:34,960
Hurry up. What for?

201
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:35,799
I'm freezing!

202
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,000
Take them off!

203
00:13:43,039 --> 00:13:43,840
Hurry up, hurry!

204
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,039
What should I do now?

205
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,720
What were you doing earlier?

206
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,600
I was watching the opera in town.

207
00:14:02,879 --> 00:14:03,840
Watching the opera?

208
00:14:04,879 --> 00:14:06,360
Then go back and keep watching.

209
00:14:06,559 --> 00:14:07,600
Remember to head back late.

210
00:14:08,759 --> 00:14:09,519
I'm leaving.

211
00:14:16,279 --> 00:14:17,519
You took the—

212
00:14:19,879 --> 00:14:21,080
You're wearing my coat.

213
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,039
I'm cold, too.

214
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:58,320
Look at his barbershop.

215
00:14:59,279 --> 00:14:59,840
In a state like this,

216
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,200
who'd dare come anymore?

217
00:15:01,879 --> 00:15:03,480
With all those knives and shears around.

218
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,279
Yeah.

219
00:15:04,759 --> 00:15:05,759
Nobody dares to step in.

220
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,559
Suspect Chen Jun,

221
00:15:07,879 --> 00:15:09,360
for the crime of murder-for-hire,

222
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,320
is sentenced to death in the first trial,

223
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,000
deprivation of political rights for life.

224
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:16,039
Liu Jianguo, for the crime of intentional homicide,

225
00:15:16,279 --> 00:15:17,679
is sentenced to death in the first trial,

226
00:15:18,159 --> 00:15:19,559
deprivation of political rights for life.

227
00:15:20,279 --> 00:15:22,200
Chen Jun's wife, Zhao Yuhong,

228
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,600
for the crime of harboring criminals,

229
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,279
sentenced to 6 months Public surveillance.

230
00:15:27,879 --> 00:15:29,399
They get to go enjoy the afterlife,

231
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,480
while we're stuck here grinding away.

232
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:40,720
Boss,

233
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,440
just over a meter-wide

234
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,480
homestead land corridor,

235
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,159
a young life in its prime

236
00:15:47,159 --> 00:15:48,200
was cut short just like that.

237
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,240
Why?

238
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,840
Don't work yourself up over it.

239
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:56,519
Xiao Chang.

240
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:57,879
I'm listening.

241
00:15:57,879 --> 00:15:58,879
I'm talking to you.

242
00:15:58,919 --> 00:15:59,799
Go ahead, Boss.

243
00:16:00,559 --> 00:16:01,639
In our line of work,

244
00:16:02,159 --> 00:16:03,000
it's like

245
00:16:04,279 --> 00:16:06,120
feeling for stones in a murky river.

246
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,720
Before you wade in,

247
00:16:09,879 --> 00:16:12,399
you think the riverbed is all solid rock,

248
00:16:12,399 --> 00:16:13,399
all firm ground.

249
00:16:16,159 --> 00:16:18,480
But once you actually step in,

250
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:19,399
you realize

251
00:16:19,639 --> 00:16:22,399
most of it down there is rotten silt.

252
00:16:24,279 --> 00:16:26,480
Built up over centuries.

253
00:16:26,519 --> 00:16:27,879
No matter how you look at it,

254
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,639
the river has its own rules,

255
00:16:32,039 --> 00:16:33,200
its own ways.

256
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,320
Understood.

257
00:16:35,639 --> 00:16:36,440
I get it.

258
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,879
After everything that's happened,

259
00:16:39,919 --> 00:16:40,840
what does it show?

260
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:46,320
It shows our legal education is lacking.

261
00:16:47,799 --> 00:16:48,960
Just like window paper,

262
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,440
it can't block the wind,

263
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:55,039
let alone the demons in people's hearts.

264
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,440
Take Chen Jun,

265
00:16:57,759 --> 00:16:58,879
and Liu Jianguo.

266
00:16:59,879 --> 00:17:01,919
Did they not know a life pays for a life?

267
00:17:02,639 --> 00:17:03,679
They knew full well.

268
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,640
Yet in that moment,

269
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,359
they didn't think it was illegal.

270
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:10,559
They thought they were just venting anger,

271
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:11,880
just settling a score.

272
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:12,680
Right.

273
00:17:13,039 --> 00:17:14,240
That's their

274
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:16,359
perfectly justified way to resolve things.

275
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:17,680
Isn't that how they see it?

276
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,279
They'd rather trust

277
00:17:19,759 --> 00:17:21,039
some quack remedy

278
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,440
than believe a doctor.

279
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,759
Even if that remedy

280
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,000
ends up killing them,

281
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:29,440
they'll still believe it.

282
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,680
That's the point.

283
00:17:33,039 --> 00:17:35,079
Like you said, sometimes they just want to blow off steam.

284
00:17:35,079 --> 00:17:36,480
Over such a petty dispute,

285
00:17:37,799 --> 00:17:39,799
what couldn't be talked out and resolved?

286
00:17:39,799 --> 00:17:41,519
If it's that big a deal, go to court.

287
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:42,920
Let the court decide.

288
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,680
Did it really have to come to murder?

289
00:17:46,799 --> 00:17:48,240
I just don't get it.

290
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:49,160
I really don't.

291
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:52,960
Honestly, though, Boss,

292
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:55,559
working this case with you these past few days,

293
00:17:55,839 --> 00:17:57,640
I've truly learned a lot.

294
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,759
And I also feel...

295
00:18:00,759 --> 00:18:01,960
I feel like I'm well-suited

296
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,880
for this line of work.

297
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:03,680
What do you think?

298
00:18:07,359 --> 00:18:08,799
You've barely scratched the surface.

299
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:12,279
There's a long road ahead of you.

300
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:14,920
Take your time to figure it out.

301
00:18:15,559 --> 00:18:17,240
Plenty of hardships are waiting for you.

302
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,799
Something happened at Chen Jun's place.
